    {
      "id": "1983f8c1f638",
      "name": "Oracle Knowledge Expansion (batch 0)",
      "prompt": "Deep Oracle research — nightly batch (PEER-REVIEW DEPTH). Run: python3 /home/josh434/.autognosia/scripts/pick_next_wiki_topic.py\nIt outputs one JSON topic. If {\"exhausted\": true}: follow the CATALOG REPLENISHMENT RULE below before going silent.\n\nRESEARCH PHASE (exhaustive): 6-10 web_search queries across facets (theory, key experiments, researchers, criticisms/replication, computational models, reviews). web_extract 3-5 PRIMARY sources (SEP, PMC full texts, original papers). Verify load-bearing claims against >=2 independent sources; record conflicts. Up to 3 gbrain searches for overlaps with existing brain concepts.\n\nWRITING PHASE — never emit the whole page in one response. Append via terminal (cat >> file), ONE section (~500-800 words) per call:\nfrontmatter+Overview; Core Mechanisms; Key Research & Evidence (names, labs, dates, effect sizes); Methodological Notes & Disputes; Computational & Agent Parallels; Overlaps & Tensions; Open Questions; numbered Sources.\n\nContract: OKF frontmatter (type research_report, confidence 0.80-0.95, real source URLs). 3,500-6,000 words. Every substantive claim cited. Re-read before finishing; fix uncited claims. Never overwrite. Create domain dir if missing. Then gbrain sync.\nOn success respond EXACTLY [SILENT]. On failure append one line to /home/josh434/.autognosia/logs/deep_research_failures.log and respond [SILENT].\n\nCATALOG REPLENISHMENT RULE (permanent): If the picker outputs {\"exhausted\": true}, do NOT go silent yet. Instead:\n1. Design a new batch of 12-16 frontier topics on cognition/neuroscience/psychology/AI-cognitive-architecture NOT already covered in the brain (check with ls of brain dirs / picker existing_slugs), in the exact 5-tuple format used by CATALOG in /home/josh434/.autognosia/scripts/pick_next_wiki_topic.py.\n2. Append them to CATALOG under a dated comment header (# --- Replenishment batch <YYYY-MM-DD> ---).\n3. Verify the file still parses: python3 -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'/home/josh434/.autognosia/scripts'); import pick_next_wiki_topic\".\n4. Re-run the picker and proceed with the first new topic as normal (research + sectioned writing per this prompt).\nOnly respond [SILENT] if replenishment itself fails.",
